# NIVEL 6 · LA IDENTIDAD · variante de maxima calidad
#
# Mantiene la tesis y la alternancia documental del guion original, pero deja
# cola de respiracion en cada toma hablada y elimina ambiguedades visuales de
# los dos B-roll que peor midieron. Las instrucciones de boca son positivas y
# contenidas: describen anatomia natural sin pedir una exhibicion de dientes.

@TIPO habla
@ESCENA A man of about fifty-five with short grey-flecked dark hair, a full soft salt-and-pepper beard that falls in soft irregular clumps, deep-set brown eyes with pronounced creases at the corners and a narrow mouth, wearing a charcoal grey wool sweater. Tight close-up: his face fills the frame from forehead to chin. A large soft diffused warm key light from the left wraps gently around his face, with soft gradual shadow on the right and no hard edges. He is seated against a plain matte black studio backdrop. Static locked-off camera, fine film grain. His restrained speech articulation remains anatomically natural: stable lips and beard, a realistically lit oral cavity, and only brief subtle glimpses of teeth when the spoken phonemes require them.
@AMBIENTE A very quiet neutral room tone with no identifiable sounds, and the clear calm male dialogue spoken by the man.
@MUSICA A single sustained low cello note held quietly and continuously, unchanging throughout.

TOMA|Un barco vuelve a puerto cada año. Y cada año le cambian una tabla podrida por una tabla nueva.|inicio|habla|
